  "answer": "If the absolute offset between instrument time and the observatory reference **exceeds two seconds**, the gateway must:\n\n1. Pause schedule execution and notify the duty operator.\n2. Keep queued reservations unchanged.\n3. Resume only after **two consecutive reference checks** report an offset within two seconds. [ev-7ff924db065d30bda70fa508, `clock.md:5–8`]\n\nIf the reference clock is unavailable, execution must remain paused; a local clock reading alone cannot satisfy either recovery check. [ev-7431ef82d2347181ffe5f433, `clock.md:9–12`]\n\nThe retired prototype’s behavior—clearing pending reservations and restarting on the first local clock sample—must not be used for the current gateway. [ev-74eb9cba956360994f654dbe, `architecture.md:9–11`]",
